  "purpose": {
    "basis": "inferred",
    "sources": [],
    "text": "Paraphrase inferred from current policy: isolated fixture git configuration."
  },
  "relations": [],
  "revisions": [
    {
      "clauses": [
        {
          "id": "clause:fb77edae2d584c87b77c032c7b3bb137",
          "offset": 2,
          "overlaps": [],
          "parent_sha256": "009a0f487e00fa3fb6962781eaaa109e842c20535fbb209a519bcca6b7f6f0e9",
          "sha256": "8577a775f5e7c1c9484a79b774de2d55783d0d4fd1013c4cd2c8011c8df43dbc",
          "text": "A test, fixture or scratch script that runs git keeps it off the host's real config\n  and repositories. Overriding `HOME` alone is not enough: with `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`\n  still exported and no `~/.gitconfig` in the new `HOME`, `git config --global` writes\n  to an existing `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/git/config`, the user's real one. Set\n  `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` to a temporary file (or `/dev/null`, with `GIT_AUTHOR_*` and\n  `GIT_COMMITTER_*` set) plus `GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1`, or override `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`\n  along with `HOME`, and prefer `git -c key=value` to `git config --global`."
        },
        {
          "id": "clause:d752936de8fb43e5aeb01766ef9447bd",
          "offset": 573,
          "overlaps": [
            "clause:6b82172a0ed341bc9113515f489de650"
          ],
          "parent_sha256": "009a0f487e00fa3fb6962781eaaa109e842c20535fbb209a519bcca6b7f6f0e9",
          "sha256": "0663ad527413375a6c866b5468f5fc8ef8fddc5a2a15999135005219259cedd2",
          "text": "A git\n  hook can export `GIT_DIR`, `GIT_INDEX_FILE` and `GIT_WORK_TREE`, which win over\n  `git -C <dir>`: unset every inherited `GIT_*` variable before building a fixture,\n  and before its first write assert both that `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` is the\n  fixture directory and that `git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir` lies inside it (with\n  only `GIT_DIR` set, the top level reads as the current directory while writes still\n  reach the real repository)."
        },
        {
          "id": "clause:6b82172a0ed341bc9113515f489de650",
          "offset": 850,
          "overlaps": [
            "clause:d752936de8fb43e5aeb01766ef9447bd"
          ],
          "parent_sha256": "009a0f487e00fa3fb6962781eaaa109e842c20535fbb209a519bcca6b7f6f0e9",
          "sha256": "bc0b3a2c31cdf4b68b5c8a29c13aa5f1ed5b6f132f1619f11301ed48c23dd79b",
          "text": "and that `git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir` lies inside it (with\n  only `GIT_DIR` set, the top level reads as the current directory while writes still\n  reach the real repository)."
        }
      ],
      "locator": {
        "kind": "git",
        "owner": "lore",
        "path": "instructions/fragments/git.md",
        "reference": "Public policy text before marker-only migration; identity bound by exact text hash.",
        "revision": "37d06342e376dec1a257b037a48ec03337de5410"
      },
      "sha256": "009a0f487e00fa3fb6962781eaaa109e842c20535fbb209a519bcca6b7f6f0e9",
      "text": "- A test, fixture or scratch script that runs git keeps it off the host's real config\n  and repositories. Overriding `HOME` alone is not enough: with `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`\n  still exported and no `~/.gitconfig` in the new `HOME`, `git config --global` writes\n  to an existing `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/git/config`, the user's real one. Set\n  `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` to a temporary file (or `/dev/null`, with `GIT_AUTHOR_*` and\n  `GIT_COMMITTER_*` set) plus `GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1`, or override `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`\n  along with `HOME`, and prefer `git -c key=value` to `git config --global`. A git\n  hook can export `GIT_DIR`, `GIT_INDEX_FILE` and `GIT_WORK_TREE`, which win over\n  `git -C <dir>`: unset every inherited `GIT_*` variable before building a fixture,\n  and before its first write assert both that `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` is the\n  fixture directory and that `git rev-parse --absolute-git-dir` lies inside it (with\n  only `GIT_DIR` set, the top level reads as the current directory while writes still\n  reach the real repository).\n"
    }
  ],
